WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.510
The smallest living things
are made of just one cell.

2
00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:07.050
They have no lungs, no
heart and no blood.

3
00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:09.990
Oxygen simply passes in
through their surface.

4
00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:11.750
You couldn't live like that.

5
00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:14.790
So what changes as living
things get bigger?

6
00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:18.190
In this mission, you'll compare
surface area with volume,

7
00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:21.440
and see what happens to
the two as an object grows.

8
00:00:21.490 --> 00:00:25.330
You'll find out why large
organisms need specialised exchange

9
00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:26.430
surfaces.

10
00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:29.430
And you'll see why they also
need a transport system,

11
00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:32.670
to link those surfaces to every cell.

12
00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:36.430
Your mission: find out why
big organisms can't rely on

13
00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:38.180
diffusion alone.
